{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1119019-mummy-how-does-the-udja-sen-purpose-works","id":1119019,"title":"Mummy: How does the Udja-sen Purpose works?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T10:16:14-07:00","id":1119019,"title":"Mummy: How does the Udja-sen Purpose works?","content":"Udja-sen Purpose allows you to add your Balance rating each time you recover Sekhem.<br /> <br /> The way I understood this, you add your Balance as a bonus, but since Balance it's the limmit to the amount of Sekhem, I don't see how can you add that much Sekhem:<br /> <br /> If I can't have more Sekhem than Balance, what's the purpose of adding your entire Balance rating?, wouldn't it always take you above your m\u00e1ximum Sekhem value?<br /> <br /> For instance. Say a character had Sekhem 1 and Balance 3. The sun rises and she gains 1 point of sekem, and because seh's an Udja-sen she sums her Balance for a total of 4 points gained.<br /> Now the character has 5 points on her reserve?, or it's increased to the limit of 3?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T09:55:22-07:00","id":1130326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy FAQ</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Under the Udja-sen Purpose it says that they get additional points of Sekhem equal to their Balance when they refresh their Sekhem, but the limit on Sekhem IS Balance. What gives?</b><br /> Actually, this is an important point. Udja-sen can recover Sekhem even when reduced to 0 Sekhem, unlike other mummies. They can also help other mummies who have reached 0 Sekhem. It is worth noting, however, that they still suffer all other effects of Semektet any time their Sekhem falls to 0. See, now they make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this answers it... Athors recognized this as a mistake, kinda. What Udja-sen CAN do it's to recover Sekhem even when reduced to 0 (and to share), this is a very potent skill if you want to play outside the Web of Faith, as they can get out of Semektet as easy as watching the sunrise (one day of Semektet ain't that bad).<br /> <br /> It doesn't seem like they can get more than the maximum Sekhem, but they may still be able to get as much as their total, which makes them a living batery compensated by the fact that using this power will hurt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-17-2017, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}